=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: leaf_router_0_1
diagnosis_text:
The BGP daemon (bgpd) on leaf_router_0_1 has crashed or been killed and is
not running, even though it is correctly enabled in /etc/frr/daemons and
has a valid configuration in frr.conf (AS 65201, advertising 10.0.1.0/24,
with neighbors toward spine_router_0_0 and spine_router_0_1). Without bgpd,
leaf_router_0_1 never establishes any eBGP sessions and never originates the
10.0.1.0/24 prefix into the fabric. Both spine_router_0_0 and spine_router_0_1
show their sessions toward leaf_router_0_1 (172.16.0.7 and 172.16.0.11
respectively) stuck in the Active state, confirming the TCP connection is
never completed. Because 10.0.1.0/24 is absent from every router's RIB —
both spines, the super-spine, and leaf_router_0_0 — pc_0_0's first-hop
gateway (leaf_router_0_0) has no route to pc_0_1's subnet and immediately
returns "Destination Net Unreachable" for every packet toward 10.0.1.2.
The team's suspicion about spine_router_0_0 is incorrect: its sessions to
super_spine_router_0 and leaf_router_0_0 are fully Established and healthy.
Root cause: bgpd is not running on leaf_router_0_1 despite being correctly
configured. Corrective fix: restart bgpd (or the full FRR service) on
leaf_router_0_1 — e.g. "service frr restart" or "bgpd -d -F traditional
--daemon -A 127.0.0.1" — which will re-establish both spine sessions,
advertise 10.0.1.0/24 fabric-wide, and restore end-to-end reachability
between pc_0_0 and pc_0_1.
=== END ===
